      {
        "text": "Now the reckoning is thus—a senine of gold, a seon of gold, a shum of gold, and a limnah of gold.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 11:5",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "A senum of silver, an amnor of silver, an ezrom of silver, and an onti of silver.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 11:6",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "A senum of silver was equal to a senine of gold, and either for a measure of barley, and also for a measure of every kind of grain.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 11:7",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Now the amount of a seon of gold was twice the value of a senine.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 11:8",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And a shum of gold was twice the value of a seon.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 11:9",
